{"id":10651,"date":"2026-06-09T12:25:15","date_gmt":"2026-06-09T12:25:15","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/?p=10651"},"modified":"2026-06-09T12:25:15","modified_gmt":"2026-06-09T12:25:15","slug":"buying-a-home-dont-skip-a-termite-inspection-in-melbourne","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/buying-a-home-dont-skip-a-termite-inspection-in-melbourne\/","title":{"rendered":"Buying a Home? Don&#8217;t Skip a Termite Inspection in Melbourne"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You have found the house. The location is great. The price feels right. The kitchen has been freshly renovated and the backyard is exactly what you wanted.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">But before you sign anything, there is one thing a lot of Melbourne home buyers skip. And it is the one thing that can cost them tens of thousands of dollars after they move in.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A termite inspection.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It sounds like something you can deal with later. It is not. Termites are one of the most destructive pests in Australia, and Melbourne properties are not immune. By the time most homeowners realise there is a problem, the damage is already done and it is expensive to fix.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you are buying a home, this is the one thing you cannot afford to skip.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2><b>Why Melbourne Homes Are at Risk<\/b><\/h2>\n<p><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone  wp-image-10653\" src=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-06-09-at-4.36.26-PM-300x200.jpeg\" alt=\"termite specialist melbourne\" width=\"1062\" height=\"708\" srcset=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-06-09-at-4.36.26-PM-300x200.jpeg 300w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-06-09-at-4.36.26-PM-1024x683.jpeg 1024w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-06-09-at-4.36.26-PM-768x512.jpeg 768w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-06-09-at-4.36.26-PM.jpeg 1536w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1062px) 100vw, 1062px\" \/><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A lot of people assume termites are only a problem in Queensland or tropical parts of Australia. That is not true.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Melbourne&#8217;s climate creates plenty of conditions that termites love. Moisture around foundations, poor drainage, ageing timber structures, and older homes that were built without any termite protection in place. Suburbs across Melbourne, from the outer east to the inner west, have properties that have been quietly damaged by termites for years without the owners even knowing.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Subterranean termites are the most common species found in Melbourne. They live underground, build mud tunnels, and work their way into timber from below. They can chew through flooring, wall frames, roof beams, and support structures while leaving the surface looking completely normal.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">That is what makes them so dangerous. You cannot see them working.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><b>What Actually Happens During a Termite Inspection<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A termite inspection is not just someone walking through your house having a quick look around. A proper <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/our-services\/termite-pest-control\/\"><b>termite inspection in Melbourne<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is a thorough check of the entire property carried out by a licensed termite specialist.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Here is what a good inspection covers.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The inspector checks all accessible areas of the property including the roof void, subfloor, internal rooms, external walls, fencing, garden beds, and any timber structures on the property like decks, pergolas, and sheds.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">They use moisture meters to detect areas of high moisture that could attract termites. Thermal imaging cameras are sometimes used to spot activity behind walls without having to open them up. Tapping tools are used to check for hollow timber, which is a classic sign that termites have been feeding inside.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At the end, you get a written report that tells you exactly what was found, where any risk areas are, and what the recommended next steps are.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">That report is something every Melbourne home buyer should have before settlement.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><b>The Real Cost of Skipping an Inspection<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Here is something worth thinking about carefully.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A termite inspection in Melbourne typically costs a few hundred dollars. It takes an hour or two. And it gives you a full picture of what you are buying.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Termite damage repair costs are a completely different story. Depending on how far the infestation has spread, repairs can run into the thousands or tens of thousands of dollars. Structural repairs to wall frames, flooring, roof timbers, and support beams are not cheap. And in serious cases, parts of the home may need to be completely rebuilt.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Home insurance in Australia generally does not cover termite damage either. It is considered a maintenance issue, not an insurable event. So if you buy a home and discover termite damage after settlement, that cost sits entirely with you.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A few hundred dollars upfront can save you a very unpleasant surprise after you move in.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><b>What to Do If Termites Are Found<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Finding termites during an inspection does not automatically mean you walk away from the property. But it does mean you need to go in with your eyes open.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If termites are discovered during an inspection, you have a few options. You can negotiate with the seller to have the termite treatment completed before settlement. You can factor the cost of termite control into your offer price. Or in some cases, if the damage is significant, you may decide the property is not worth the risk.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The key is that you know before you sign. That is the whole point of the inspection.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Once you do own the property, whether termites were found or not, putting a proper termite management plan in place is the smart move. This usually involves installing a termite barrier system around the perimeter of the property and scheduling annual termite inspections to catch any future activity early.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><b>What Is a Termite Barrier and Do You Need One<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A termite barrier is one of the most effective ways to protect a Melbourne property long term.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">There are two main types. A chemical termite barrier involves treating the soil around and under the property with a product that either kills termites on contact or is carried back to the colony. A physical termite barrier is usually installed during construction and involves a layer of material that termites cannot pass through.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For existing homes, a chemical barrier is the most common solution. It is applied around the full perimeter of the property and under the slab where possible. When it is installed correctly by a licensed termite specialist, it provides solid long-term protection.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Most termite barriers need to be reapplied or inspected every few years to remain effective, which is why ongoing termite management in Melbourne is important rather than treating it as a one-off solution.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><b>Signs to Watch for When Inspecting a Property Yourself<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Even before you book a professional inspection, there are a few things worth looking for when you walk through a property.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Mud tubes along walls, foundations, or inside cupboards are a strong indicator of subterranean termite activity. These are small tunnels made of soil and timber particles that termites build to travel between the ground and their food source.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Timber that sounds hollow when you knock on it is another warning sign. Termites eat timber from the inside, leaving a thin shell behind that collapses when pressed.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Doors and windows that have started to stick or warp without an obvious reason can sometimes be caused by termite damage affecting the surrounding frames.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Small piles of what looks like sawdust or tiny pellets near timber structures can also indicate activity.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you spot any of these things during a property walkthrough, make sure a qualified<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/our-services\/termite-pest-control\/\"><b> termite specialist in Melbourne<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> takes a proper look before you go any further.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><b>Getting the Right Help in Melbourne\u00a0<\/b><\/h3>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone  wp-image-10652\" src=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-06-09-at-4.36.26-PM-1-300x200.jpeg\" alt=\"termite specialist melbourne\" width=\"818\" height=\"545\" srcset=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-06-09-at-4.36.26-PM-1-300x200.jpeg 300w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-06-09-at-4.36.26-PM-1-1024x683.jpeg 1024w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-06-09-at-4.36.26-PM-1-768x512.jpeg 768w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-06-09-at-4.36.26-PM-1.jpeg 1536w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 818px) 100vw, 818px\" \/><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Not all pest inspectors are the same. When you are booking a termite inspection for a property purchase, make sure the person carrying it out is properly licensed and experienced in termite identification and assessment.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/\"><b>7 States Pest Control, <\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">our team carries out thorough termite inspections across Melbourne for home buyers, property owners, and real estate transactions. We give you a clear, detailed report with no jargon and no upselling. Just honest advice about what we found and what your options are.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Whether you need a pre-purchase termite inspection, a termite barrier installed, or ongoing termite management for a property you already own, we can help.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Call us on <\/span><a href=\"tel:+61434660060\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">+61 434 660 060 <\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0to book your inspection.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Looking for reliable<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/\"> <b>pest control Melbourne<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> services ? We provide complete solutions including<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/our-services\/spider-control-treatment-melbourne\/\"> <b>spider control services<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/our-services\/spider-control-treatment-melbourne\/\"> <b>spider removal service<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to keep your property safe. Our experts also handle<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/our-services\/fox-pest-control-in-melbourne\/\"> <b>fox population control<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/our-services\/possum-pest-control\/\"> <b>possum removal service Melbourne<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. For long-term protection, we offer<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/our-services\/termite-pest-control\/\"> <b>termite control Melbourne<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and effective<\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/our-services\/termite-pest-control\/\"> <b>termite treatment Melbourne<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.<\/span><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>You have found the house. The location is great. The price feels right. The kitchen has been freshly renovated and the backyard is exactly what you wanted. But before you sign anything, there is one thing a lot of Melbourne home buyers skip. And it is the one thing that can cost them tens of [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":10654,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[1],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-10651","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-blog"],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v25.4 - https:\/\/yoast.com\/wordpress\/plugins\/seo\/ -->\n<title>Termite Inspection Melbourne | Home Buyers Guide<\/title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Buying a home in Melbourne? Never skip a termite inspection. Learn what termite inspections cover, what they cost, and how to protect your investment today.\" \/>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/buying-a-home-dont-skip-a-termite-inspection-in-melbourne\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Termite Inspection Melbourne | Home Buyers Guide\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Buying a home in Melbourne? Never skip a termite inspection. Learn what termite inspections cover, what they cost, and how to protect your investment today.\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/buying-a-home-dont-skip-a-termite-inspection-in-melbourne\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"7 States Pest Control\" \/>\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2026-06-09T12:25:15+00:00\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-06-09-at-4.35.58-PM.jpeg\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1200\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"630\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image\/jpeg\" \/>\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"7 States Pest Control\" \/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" \/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"7 States Pest Control\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"7 minutes\" \/>\n<script type=\"application\/ld+json\" class=\"yoast-schema-graph\">{\"@context\":\"https:\/\/schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@type\":\"Article\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/buying-a-home-dont-skip-a-termite-inspection-in-melbourne\/#article\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/buying-a-home-dont-skip-a-termite-inspection-in-melbourne\/\"},\"author\":{\"name\":\"7 States Pest Control\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/#\/schema\/person\/d2eebd8e6e8b6f07170a10bc11d3dadb\"},\"headline\":\"Buying a Home? Don&#8217;t Skip a Termite Inspection in Melbourne\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-06-09T12:25:15+00:00\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/buying-a-home-dont-skip-a-termite-inspection-in-melbourne\/\"},\"wordCount\":1257,\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/#organization\"},\"image\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/buying-a-home-dont-skip-a-termite-inspection-in-melbourne\/#primaryimage\"},\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-06-09-at-4.35.58-PM.jpeg\",\"articleSection\":[\"Blog\"],\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/buying-a-home-dont-skip-a-termite-inspection-in-melbourne\/\",\"url\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/buying-a-home-dont-skip-a-termite-inspection-in-melbourne\/\",\"name\":\"Termite Inspection Melbourne | Home Buyers Guide\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/#website\"},\"primaryImageOfPage\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/buying-a-home-dont-skip-a-termite-inspection-in-melbourne\/#primaryimage\"},\"image\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/buying-a-home-dont-skip-a-termite-inspection-in-melbourne\/#primaryimage\"},\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-06-09-at-4.35.58-PM.jpeg\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-06-09T12:25:15+00:00\",\"description\":\"Buying a home in Melbourne? Never skip a termite inspection. Learn what termite inspections cover, what they cost, and how to protect your investment today.\",\"breadcrumb\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/buying-a-home-dont-skip-a-termite-inspection-in-melbourne\/#breadcrumb\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"potentialAction\":[{\"@type\":\"ReadAction\",\"target\":[\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/buying-a-home-dont-skip-a-termite-inspection-in-melbourne\/\"]}]},{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/buying-a-home-dont-skip-a-termite-inspection-in-melbourne\/#primaryimage\",\"url\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-06-09-at-4.35.58-PM.jpeg\",\"contentUrl\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/WhatsApp-Image-2026-06-09-at-4.35.58-PM.jpeg\",\"width\":1200,\"height\":630,\"caption\":\"termite specialist melbourne\"},{\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/buying-a-home-dont-skip-a-termite-inspection-in-melbourne\/#breadcrumb\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Buying a Home? Don&#8217;t Skip a Termite Inspection in Melbourne\"}]},{\"@type\":\"WebSite\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/#website\",\"url\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/\",\"name\":\"7 States Pest Control\",\"description\":\"\",\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/#organization\"},\"potentialAction\":[{\"@type\":\"SearchAction\",\"target\":{\"@type\":\"EntryPoint\",\"urlTemplate\":\"htt